#%PAM-1.0
# Fingerprint-only service used by the greeter for its background / empty-
# password attempt. `requisite` ends the auth stack the moment pam_fprintd
# fails, so a fingerprint miss (or a timeout, or a "device already claimed"
# error) can never fall through into pam_unix with an empty password. That
# fall-through was a pam_faillock strike each time: three fingerprint misses
# locked the account, and then the correct password was silently rejected
# for ten minutes (2026-08-17). No system-local-login include on purpose.

auth       requisite    pam_fprintd.so

account    include      system-local-login

session    include      system-local-login
